ntdll's startup on wasm64 (docs/design/wine-unix.md, section 8; section 3
for the CPU).

boot (native/wine/src/boot.c) runs __wine_main as the exec'd wine loader
would; these are the changes the startup path needs.
- Paths (loader.c, init_paths): no dladdr. ntdll.so's directory is the
  constant LIBDIR "/wine/x86_64-unix", so the PE files are under
  /wine/lib/wine/x86_64-windows, NLS and wine.inf under /wine/share/wine
  and the loader in /wine/bin, in MEMFS.
- The host-pointer slots in ntdll.dll (loader.c, load_ntdll_functions):
  __wine_syscall_dispatcher and __wine_unix_call_dispatcher get the
  poison value TW_NO_DISPATCHER until M3; __wine_unixlib_handle gets the
  host address of unix_call_funcs, an opaque handle.
- The initial directory (env.c, get_initial_directory): the launch
  directory boot recorded, not getcwd(), which the in-process server
  has moved.
- The wineboot skip (env.c, run_wineboot): no wineboot process. It
  creates \KernelObjects\__wineboot_event, initializes KUSER, writes
  wineboot's seven KUSER fields (create_user_shared_data) from the
  version, sets the event and waits on it as Wine does.
- No child processes (process.c, NtCreateUserProcess): it prints
  "tempwind: unsupported: NtCreateUserProcess <image>" and returns
  STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED.
- The CPU (system.c, section 3): do_cpuid reads the translator's profile
  (TW_CPUID_LEAVES, zeros for other leaves), do_xgetbv returns TW_XCR0,
  the DAZ probe reads TW_MXCSR_MASK, and there is one processor. This
  replaces 0002's loud stops.

